{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta New Admin Console Behaviours",
  "Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1078.004\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta New Admin Console Behaviours\" or \"<ip>|Okta New Admin Console Behaviours\"\n\nDetects sign-on policy evaluations (policy.evaluate_sign_on) for the Okta Admin Console where Okta flags a new geo-location, device, IP, country, city, state, or velocity. Okta reports behaviors in two fields with different formats (debugData.behaviors 'New Device=POSITIVE' and logOnlySecurityData '\"New Device\":\"POSITIVE\"'); either one counts. The alert lists the behaviors that fired. Risk floor High (75).\n\nFalse positives: an administrator on a new laptop or travelling. Tune with okta_user_allowlist.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_new_behaviours_admin_console/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/?query=okta.yml",
